<http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/NodeShape/CoachLayoutDescriptionType/LayoutNT/GridSize> a sh:NodeShape ;
    era:usedInTelematics true ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-02T13:08:22+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:references "https://gitlab.com/era-europa-eu/public/era-telematics-tsi/tsi_telematics/-/blob/V4.0.0/TD_B5_A2_xsd/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    sh:description """Items are places within the grid. 

The granularity of the grid can be finer that the number of places in a row.

A good choice for the vertical grid size would be 25 for coaches up to 4 places in a row and 30 in case of 5 places in a row. The graphical elements for places and icons are approximately of size 5 x 5, so they have a well defined center at (3,3). In any case the size should be even to provide a well defined center.

Graphical items for places and icons should be sized to have an empty frame around them to show underlying compartment walls.
"""@en,
        """Total size of the grid that contains all graphical items. All items listed must be within the grid. 

The Corners of the grid are:

  upper left corner:            (0,0)
  upper right corned:         (0,y)
  lower left corner:            (x,0)
  lower right cormner:       (x,y)


Items are places within the grid. 

The granularity of the grid can be finer that the number of places in a row.

A good choice for the vertical grid size would be 25 for coaches up to 4 places in a row and 30 in case of 5 places in a row. The graphical elements for places and icons are approximately of size 5 x 5, so they have a well defined center at (3,3). In any case the size should be even to provide a well defined center.

Graphical items for places and icons should be sized to have an empty frame around them to show underlying compartment walls.
"""@en ;
    sh:name "Grid size"@en ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
    sh:property <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/PropertyShape/CoachLayoutDescriptionType/LayoutNT/GridSize/x>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/PropertyShape/CoachLayoutDescriptionType/LayoutNT/GridSize/y> ;
    sh:targetClass era:GridSize .

